{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008777-hack-second-inferior-arcanum","id":1008777,"title":"[Hack] Second Inferior Arcanum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T20:05:05-08:00","id":1008777,"title":"[Hack] Second Inferior Arcanum","content":"Legacies, wonderful splats that adds character to magic, along with several mechanical benefits. Unfortunately, one of these benefits can result in a mage not having any Inferior Arcanum, and that seems a little over-powered to me. Solution: Paths have a second Inferior Arcanum. It also makes for some nice symmetry of the Ruling Arcana. But what should these Inferior Arcana be? Here are my suggestions:<br /> <br /> <b>Acanthus - Prime</b><br /> Arcadia is a realm of many perspectives and wills, with oaths weaving everything together. Fate is fickle and Time waits for no one. Who are the witches to dictate what is absolute and reject all nuance? They coax and barter the Arcana to do their bidding, they don't command them. Prime requires command and for the mage to be absolute in their spells before it listens, however.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastigos - Life</b><br /> From a warlock's perspective, magic is internal, not external. Magic comes from the soul, thus it is for the soul. The body is to be refined and sculpted by the body's means. Besides, Life is all instinct and no thought, and those who try to scour such base urges don't tend to revel in them.<br /> <br /> <b>Moros - Space</b><br /> When a soul departs from the Fallen World, it loses all of its attachments to it. All of a person's relations and identity are stripped bare in Stygia, leaving all its riches to the Crypts to begin anew. Everyone comes and goes, many times suddenly, so why concern yourself of such attachments?<br /> <br /> <b>Obrimos - Fate</b><br /> Fate, though it may be a chaotic Arcanum, it is also a subtle one. It doesn't like being pushed and determined as its gross cousin Forces demands to be. It wants mages to negotiate with it, ask it for a favor and give something in return. Thaumaturges have a hard time with that, considering the Aether is a realm of might and truth that threatens to destroy those eager to please or with weak convictions.<br /> <br /> <b>Thrysus - Time</b><br /> Beasts of the Primal Wild live in the moment. Every waking moment of every day of their lives are under constant threat of predation and hazards. There's simply no time for rest or reflection, only constant strife. Shamans deal with the echoes of such a restless existence daily, seeing that dog eat dog world reflected in the Fallen World. What good is seeing the past or future when you're living in the present?<br /> <br /> In addition, I also suggest the maximum dots a mage can learn Arcana dots untrained is the same 5 for Ruling, 3 for Common, and 1 for Inferior. The rationale behind this is because the real power of an Arcanum starts coming out at 4 dots, so limiting Common to 3 means they can have a substantial amount of power, but only start getting really good if they're taught (or it becomes a Ruling). For Inferior at 1 dot, it brings a bit of extra difficulty to make it a Ruling Arcanum through a Legacy, since you need it at 2 dots for initiation.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T20:46:10-08:00","id":1008787,"title":"","content":"Eh, whatever works for you. I don't think it's overpowered to end up with a non-Inferior arcana though. You can't start with dots in your Inferior arcana which means you will have to spend more XP than a person who isn't eliminating their Inferior arcana before getting into the legacy you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T22:02:51-08:00","id":1008814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008777-hack-second-inferior-arcanum?p=1008787#post1008787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, whatever works for you. I don't think it's overpowered to end up with a non-Inferior arcana though. You can't start with dots in your Inferior arcana which means you will have to spend more XP than a person who isn't eliminating their Inferior arcana before getting into the legacy you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and the necessary requirement of spending mana for every single improvised spell of non-ruling arcana makes the restrictions on inferior mostly irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T03:14:30-08:00","id":1009258,"title":"","content":"Inferior Arcana are more of a ribbon mechanic than anything, honestly. You could have 5 and you could have 0 Inferior Arcana and not an inch of difference in a power level of majority of mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}